.TH IRDIFF 1 "2026-10-26" "irdiff 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
irdiff \- compare LLVM IR and explain optimization changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irdiff
.RB [ diff ]
.I A B
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B irdiff passes
.I input
.RB [ \-p
.IR pipeline " | " \-O N ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B irdiff passes \-\-from\-log
.I log
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B irdiff pipelines
.I input
.B \-a
.I pipeline
.B \-b
.I pipeline
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B irdiff analyze
.I input
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B irdiff investigate
.I A B
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B irdiff
compares two LLVM IR snapshots (textual
.I .ll
or bitcode
.IR .bc )
and reports added, removed, modified, moved, merged and split blocks and
instructions, control-flow and loop changes, and changes to signatures,
attributes, linkage, globals, declarations and module properties.
Value names, block labels, metadata and attribute-group numbering, block
layout and other non-semantic differences are normalized away.
.PP
.B passes
runs a pass pipeline with LLVM's new pass manager and attributes each change
to the pass execution that made it, or replays an existing
.B \-print\-after\-all
or
.B \-print\-changed
log produced with
.BR \-print\-module\-scope .
.B pipelines
runs two pipelines or target configurations and compares the results,
optimization remarks and pass sequences.
.B analyze
prints dominator, loop, scalar-evolution, alias-analysis and MemorySSA facts.
.B investigate
is
.B diff
with analyses, remarks and evidence-backed hints.
.PP
An input of
.B \-
reads standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format =\fItext\fR|\fIunified\fR|\fIside\-by\-side\fR|\fIjson\fR
Output format; default text.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show all details, significance labels and full listings.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing; set the exit status only.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Print summary statistics only.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-context =\fIN\fR
Context lines for unified and side-by-side output (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-width= N
Width of side-by-side output (default $COLUMNS or 160).
.TP
.BR \-\-names =\fIoriginal\fR|\fIcanonical\fR
Show original value names, or normalized names shared by matched values.
.TP
.BR \-\-color [=\fIauto\fR|\fIalways\fR|\fInever\fR] ", " \-\-no\-color
Colorize text output. auto honours NO_COLOR and TERM=dumb.
.TP
.BR \-\-fail\-on =\fIany\fR|\fIminor\fR|\fImajor\fR|\fInever\fR
Which shown changes make the exit status 1 (default any).
.TP
.B \-\-hints
List potentially relevant differences with their evidence.
.SS Filtering
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-function =\fIglob\fR
Only functions matching
.I glob
(repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-block= glob
Only changes in matching blocks.
.TP
.BI \-\-category= list
Only these categories (see
.BR \-\-list\-categories ).
.TP
.BI \-\-change= list
Only these change kinds.
.TP
.BI \-\-pass= glob
Only pass steps whose class or pipeline name matches.
.TP
.BI \-\-analysis= list
Analyses to run and report: dom, loops, scev, aa, mssa.
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-significance =\fIcosmetic\fR|\fIminor\fR|\fImajor\fR
Hide changes below this level (default minor).
.B \-\-all
equals cosmetic,
.B \-\-major
equals major.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-categories
List categories, kinds and analyses.
.SS Normalization
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-info
Compare debug locations and variable records.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-metadata
Ignore non-debug metadata attachments.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-attributes
Ignore attribute differences.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Report layout and source_filename changes as minor.
.SS Input and pipelines
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Do not run the IR verifier on inputs.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-compatible
Exit 4 if target triples or data layouts differ.
.TP
.B \-\-analyses
Also compare analysis results (diff).
.TP
.BI \-\-aa\-limit= N
Loads and stores per function used for alias queries (default 48).
.TP
.BI \-\-remarks\-a= file ", " \-\-remarks\-b= file
Optimization remarks (YAML or bitstream) for each side.
.TP
.BI \-p " pipeline"
Pipeline in opt \-passes syntax (default default<O2>).
.TP
.BR \-O0 ", " \-O1 ", " \-O2 ", " \-O3 ", " \-Os ", " \-Oz
Shorthand for \-p default<ON>.
.TP
.BI \-a " pipeline" ", " \-b " pipeline"
Pipelines for the two sides of
.BR pipelines .
.TP
.BI \-\-mcpu= cpu ", " \-\-mattr= features
Target CPU and features;
.B \-\-mcpu\-b
and
.B \-\-mattr\-b
override side B of
.BR pipelines .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-target
Use target-independent cost models.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-each\-pass
Verify the IR after every pass.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-snapshots= dir
Write the module after every changing pass.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-log= file
Replay a module-scoped pass log.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No differences shown.
.TP
.B 1
Differences shown (see \-\-fail\-on).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Unreadable, malformed or invalid input.
.TP
.B 4
Incompatible input, for example bitcode from a newer LLVM, or differing
targets with \-\-require\-compatible.
.TP
.B 5
Internal error or pipeline failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
irdiff before.ll after.ll
irdiff before.bc after.bc \-f unified \-U 5
irdiff a.ll b.ll \-\-major \-\-fail\-on=major \-q
irdiff passes x.ll \-O2 \-F hot \-\-pass='licm*'
irdiff pipelines x.ll \-a 'default<O2>' \-b 'default<O3>'
irdiff investigate o2.ll o3.ll \-\-remarks\-a o2.yaml \-\-remarks\-b o3.yaml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opt (1),
.BR clang (1),
.BR llvm\-diff (1)
.PP
The full manual is docs/manual.md in the source distribution.
